  "seoTitle": "Sufmi Dasco Ahmad Eyed as Potential Vice President",
  "metaDescription": "Sufmi Dasco Ahmad receives support from various political and labor groups as a potential candidate for the Indonesian vice presidency.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "Deputy House Speaker Sufmi Dasco Ahmad is being discussed as a potential candidate for Vice President to succeed Gibran Rakabuming Raka.",
    "Proponents cite his ability to maintain political stability and his track record of working with diverse groups including labor organizations.",
    "Dasco has responded to the growing support by urging the public to respect the presidential prerogative in selecting a vice president."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The nomination of Deputy House Speaker Sufmi Dasco Ahmad as a potential Vice President has gained significant traction among various political factions and labor groups in Indonesia. Supporters, including elements within the NasDem party and the Prosperous Justice Party (PKS), as well as the All-Indonesian Workers Union (KSPSI), argue that Dasco possesses the temperament and political experience necessary to support President Prabowo Subianto. Proponents emphasize his alleged ability to bridge divides and ensure governmental stability. Locally, various branches of the Gerindra party have also publicly voiced their approval, characterizing him as a leader who prioritizes national interest over personal ambition. In response to the ongoing discourse regarding his potential candidacy, Dasco has publicly stated that the selection of a vice president is a matter of presidential authority and has called on all parties to respect that established process.",
